From 7301e3c83b03c12bbce5d057f285a6af4cb4259a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Peavey <sunmachine@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:47:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Prototype: raymarched voxel smoke (C_NeoVolSmoke +
 Neo_VolSmoke shader)

Order-independent smoke without OIT: each smoke volume is a CPU voxel grid
rendered as ONE raymarched box, so transmittance is integrated along the eye
ray and nothing inside the volume ever needs sorting.

Client (game/client/neo/c_neo_volsmoke.*):
- Flood-fills a 32^3 (16/64 selectable) grid through world collision using
  enginetrace, spread over frames for the bloom animation. Gas budget is a
  fraction of the inscribed sphere, so in corridors it spreads further.
- Per-cell ramp, carve/regrow (bullets, explosions) and end-of-life fade.
- Slab-ordered light sweep toward neo_volsmoke_lightdir -> per-voxel
  transmittance baked into the G channel.
- Uploads R=density, G=light as a 2D slice atlas via a procedural texture
  (material system has no 3D procedural textures).
- Draws the AABB's far faces only with the hardware depth test off; the pixel
  shader clips against the engine's depth-in-dest-alpha frame buffer copy,
  which is what spritecard $DEPTHBLEND already reads.
- Optional hook (neo_volsmoke_hook_grenade 1) replaces the legacy
  C_ParticleSmokeGrenade billboard smoke on grenade detonation.

Shader (materialsystem/stdshaders/Neo_VolSmoke.cpp, neo_volsmoke_{vs,ps}30.fxc):
- ps_3_0 dynamic loop, manual trilinear between atlas slices, animated value
  noise edge erosion, interleaved-gradient jitter, premultiplied output.
- Clip Z is affine along the ray, so the depth compare needs no extra matrices:
  the VS hands the PS clip Z at the vertex and at the eye.

Console: neo_volsmoke_spawn [extent] [lifetime], neo_volsmoke_carve,
neo_volsmoke_explode, neo_volsmoke_clear, neo_volsmoke_debug 0..3,
neo_volsmoke_cullflip (toggle if smoke vanishes when you stand inside it).

The .inc files are hand-written to match the generator's output; run
buildneoshaders.bat to produce the .vcs files (they ship via neoAssets).
